oss4 (4.2-build2020-10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * This fork adds working audio support for the Lenovo ThinkPad P70
    (Intel SPT/KBL-LP HDA controller 8086:9d71 + Realtek ALC298 codec)
  * oss_hdaudio: support modern Intel HDA controllers (SKL/KBL/CNL/CML/
    ICL/TGL/ADL/RPL/APL/GML + earlier HSW/BDW/BYT/BSW) and Realtek ALC298
  * Fix DMA under IOMMU (dma_alloc_attrs with va->dma table, table-driven
    free for vmix subdevices), codec vendor probe, RIRB state reset
  * Verified working on Debian 13 kernel 6.12.101 (ALC298 on ThinkPad,
    audio plays via /dev/dsp)

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@riseup.net>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 02:05:00 +0000

oss4 (4.2-build2020-9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase Debian packaging on deb-multimedia (Christian Marillat) oss4-dmo:
    restore oss4-base, oss4-gtk, oss4-dkms, oss4-source, oss4-dev packages
    with kernel driver build (dkms) and modern-kernel patch set applied
    in-tree (mregparm guard, linux/io, proc_ops, time_t, kernel includes,
    module symbols for >= 6.2).
  * oss4-dkms: enable oss_usb driver (USB audio, required for radio
    sound card use); exclude lynxtwo from the dkms tree.
  * liboss4-salsa-dev: enable on Linux (linux-any).

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@riseup.net>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0000

oss4 (4.2-build2020-8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * liboss4-salsa-dev: Enable on Linux (linux-any). The package conflicts
    with libasound2-dev by design; install only on OSS-exclusive systems.

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@riseup.net>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 13:00:00 +0000

oss4 (4.2-build2020-7) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fork update: apply Debian libsalsa patch set directly in-tree and
    remove debian/patches (quilt series no longer used).
  * Include Arch Linux AUR kernel-compat fixes (osscore, ossvermagic,
    extramodules, soundon, rm-init-scripts, remove-hal).

 -- Rafael Diniz <rafael@riseup.net>  Fri, 07 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
  * patches/101_use_env_CFLAGS.patch: Fix taking CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS into
    account.
  * Update standards version to 4.6.2, no changes needed.
  * rules: Simplify and rewrite to use debhelper instead of cdbs
    (Closes: Bug#1111846)

 -- Samuel Thibault <sthibault@debian.org>  Fri, 22 Aug 2025 22:57:18 +0200

oss4 (4.2-build2020-5) unstable; urgency=medium

